$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A portion of the solution (0.67 mL, 1.00 mmol)
was added to a solution of KOt-Bu (78 mg, 0.70 mmol) in i-BuOH (74 mg,
1.0 mmol) in a 6-mL vial. The resulting mixture was stirred at r.t. for
45 min. A solution of NiCl2.glyme (4.4 mg, 0.02 mmol) and (2R,
2’R)-(-)-2, 2’-Bipyrrolidine (3.4 mg, 0.024 mmol) in i-Pr2O (0.4 mL) in a
10-mL vial was stirred at r.t. for 1 h. Next, a solution of the
electrophile (0.20 mmol) in i-Pr2O (0.5 mL) was added, along with i-Pr2O
rinsing (0.5 mL) (Note: if the electrophile is solid, then it was added
as a solid, followed by 1.5 mL of i-Pr2O), and then the solution of the
activated trialkylborane was added which adjust the total volume to 4.0
mL. The reaction mixture was stirred at r.t, and then it was filtered
through silica gel, eluting with Et2O (20 mL). The solvent was removed by
rotary evaporation, and the residue was purified by chromatography. For
the product that contained sulfonamide, after purification through the
silica gel column, C18-reversed phase silica gel (water/acetonitrile
10-100%) was needed. The corresponding compound.
(S)-(2-fluoropentane-1,5-diyl)dibenzene2 .
(S)-4-fluoro-5-phenyl-N-((R)-1-phenylethyl)pentanamide. 83%; light yellow
solide. IR (neat) 3075, 2974, 1290, 782, 466; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ
7.40-7.16 (m, 10H), 6.19 (s, broad, 1H), 4.83-4.50 (m, 1H), 2.99-2.75 (m,
2H), 2.41-2.20 (m, 2H), 2.01-1.83 (m, 2H), 1.44 (d, J = 6.9 Hz,3H) ; 13C
NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 171.2, 143.3, 136.9, 136.8, 129.3, 128.5, 127.2,
126.5, 126.0, 94.8 (d, J = 170.1 Hz), 48.7, 41.7 (d, J = 21.1 Hz), 31.9
(d, J = 3.8 Hz), 30.6, 21.8; 19F NMR (CDCl3, 188 MHz): δ -180.7; HRMS
(ESI) calcd for C19H122FNNaO [M+Na]+: 322.1591; found: 322.1596.
