$DATUM BT-alanine(14) Diisopropylethylamine (0.068 mL, 0.388 mmol) and HATU
(0.492 g, 1.29 mmol) was added to a well-stirred solution of 13 (0.1 g,
0.323 mmol) in a mixture of DCM (3 mL) and DMF (0.3 mL) under N2. After
the mixture was stirred for 1 h, (S)-2-amino-N-methylpropanamide (0.132
g, 1.29 mmol) dissolved in a mixture of DMF (0.9 mL) and DCM (0.3 mL) was
added to the reaction mixture. The resulting solution was stirred for 2
h. The reaction mixture was then poured into 0.1M aqueous HCl (10 mL),
and the product was extracted with DCM. The organic layer was dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated under reduced pressure. silica gel
(DCM/MeOH, 20/1). 14 as a white solid (0.102 g, 79%). Mp: 52-53 °C; [α]D
25 = -6.3 (c = 0.1, CHCl3); 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) [ppm] 1.52 (d, J =
6.9 Hz, 3H). 2.13 (m, 2H), 2.81 (d, J = 5.0 Hz, 3H), 4.26 (m, 2H),
4.40(m, 2H), 4.73 (td, J = 7.1, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 6.58 (m, 2H), 6.70 (bs, 1H),
7.11 (m, 1H), 7.25 (m, 2H), 7.32 (dd, J = 7.9, 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.67 (d, J =
7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.84 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H); 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) [ppm]
18.6, 26.6, 30.6, 50.1, 70.0, 70.2, 93.5, 95.4, 103.9, 112.3, 112.9,
115.9, 125.1, 125.3, 129.5, 131.2, 135.4, 147.3, 161.5, 162.4, 166.6,
173.4; HRMS-ESI: m/z [M + Na]+ calcd for C22H23N3O4Na: 416.1586; found:
416.1588. abs λ max = 345; ε: 10386; em λ max = 456.
